        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-ba-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Say what happens to a known object",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Put a specific, identifiable object after 把, then say what you do to it or where it ends up. The predicate needs useful information such as a result or location; 把 is not a replacement for every object sentence.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "请把那本书放在桌子旁边。",
                "pinyin": "qǐng bǎ nà běn shū fàng zài zhuōzi pángbiān 。",
                "meaning": "Please put that book beside the desk.",
                "audio": "8cfc9f2b37951dc51b043e0d6d5cac71c37acef7a93dfaf93b154ed8c165824f"
              }
            ]
